# Retrieving Interfaces from a GraphQL Endpoint

There are several ways to retrieve interface definitions from a GraphQL endpoint:

## 1. Using Introspection Query

GraphQL has a built-in introspection system. You can query for interfaces directly:

```graphql
query GetInterfaces {
  __schema {
    types {
      kind
      name
      description
      possibleTypes {
        name
      }
      fields {
        name
        type {
          name
          kind
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### Filter specifically for interfaces:

```graphql
query GetInterfacesOnly {
  __schema {
    types(filter: { kind: INTERFACE }) {
      name
      description
      fields {
        name
        type {
          name
        }
      }
      possibleTypes {
        name
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## 2. Using cURL

```bash
curl -X POST \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"query": "{ __schema { types { kind name fields { name } possibleTypes { name } } } }"}' \
  https://your-graphql-endpoint.com/graphql
```

## 3. Using JavaScript/Fetch

```javascript
const query = `
  query {
    __schema {
      types {
        kind
        name
        fields {
          name
        }
        possibleTypes {
          name
        }
      }
    }
  }
`;

fetch('https://your-graphql-endpoint.com/graphql', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({ query })
})
  .then(res => res.json())
  .then(data => {
    // Filter for interfaces only
    const interfaces = data.data.__schema.types.filter(
      type => type.kind === 'INTERFACE'
    );
    console.log(interfaces);
  });
```

## 4. Using GraphQL Tools/IDEs

| Tool | How to Access |
|------|---------------|
| **GraphiQL** | Use the "Docs" sidebar panel |
| **Apollo Studio** | Schema > Types > Filter by Interface |
| **Postman** | Schema tab after connecting |
| **Insomnia** | Show Documentation sidebar |

## 5. Using Apollo Client (getIntrospectionQuery)

```javascript
import { getIntrospectionQuery } from 'graphql';

const introspectionQuery = getIntrospectionQuery();
// Send this query to your endpoint
```

## Example Response

```json
{
  "data": {
    "__schema": {
      "types": [
        {
          "kind": "INTERFACE",
          "name": "Node",
          "fields": [
            { "name": "id", "type": { "name": "ID" } }
          ],
          "possibleTypes": [
            { "name": "User" },
            { "name": "Post" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

> ⚠️ **Note:** Some GraphQL servers disable introspection in production for security reasons. If you get an error, check with the API provider.

